module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjLargeDegrees.CokernelModule

/-!
# Tag 0AG7 for a graded ring generated in degree one

Let `A = ⨁_{d ≥ 0} 𝒜 d` be a graded ring with `𝒜 0` Noetherian, generated over `𝒜 0` by finitely
many elements of `𝒜 1`, and let `M` be a finite graded `A`-module, `X = Proj A`. Then the
canonical maps

`𝒨 n ⟶ Γ(X, M(n)~)`

of Equation 01MR are bijective in all sufficiently large degrees. This is [Stacks, Tag 0AG7], and
it is the case to which [Stacks, Tag 0B5R] part (5) reduces the general one by the Veronese trick.

The proof is
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjLargeDegreeSections.exists_bijective_degreeNToGlobalSections`
with both halves of its homogeneous generating data supplied:
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjLargeDegrees.exists_kernel_data` for the kernel and
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjLargeDegrees.exists_cokernel_data` for the cokernel.

## Main results

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjLargeDegrees.exists_bijective_degreeNToGlobalSections_degreeOne`:
  **[Stacks, Tag 0AG7]**, with both halves of the generating data discharged.

## Implementation notes

No `stacks` attribute is attached. The tag's site in the repository is
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjLargeDegreeSections.exists_bijective_degreeNToGlobalSections`,
whose attribute describes the statement with the generating data assumed; what this file adds is
that both halves of that data are dischargeable from the source's own hypotheses once the ring is
generated in degree one.

The generating family is taken over an arbitrary `Fin nx`, including the empty family — that is
the case `A = 𝒜 0` and `Proj A = ∅` — and padded to `Fin (m + 1 + 1)` by
`Stacks.ProjCoherentDegreeOne.exists_two_le_generators` where the imported finiteness statement
asks for it.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0AG7](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0AG7)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B5R](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B5R)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory Opposite TopologicalSpace DirectSum
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjShiftedSections
  (shiftedSectionsComponent degreeNToGlobalSections)
open scoped Stacks.GradedLocalization

namespace Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjLargeDegrees

universe u

variable {A : Type u} {M : Type u} {σ : Type u} {τ : Type u}
  [CommRing A] [AddCommGroup M] [Module A M]
  [SetLike σ A] [AddSubgroupClass σ A] (𝒜 : ℕ → σ) [GradedRing 𝒜]
  [SetLike τ M] [AddSubgroupClass τ M] (𝒨 : ℤ → τ) [DirectSum.Decomposition 𝒨]
  [SetLike.GradedSMul 𝒜 𝒨]

/-- **[Stacks, Tag 0AG7].** Let `A = ⨁_{d ≥ 0} 𝒜 d` be a graded ring whose degree-zero part is
Noetherian and which is generated over it by finitely many elements of `𝒜 1`, and let `M` be a
finite graded `A`-module. Then the canonical maps `𝒨 n ⟶ Γ(Proj 𝒜, M(n)~)` of Equation 01MR are
bijective in all sufficiently large degrees.

Both halves of the homogeneous generating data of
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjLargeDegreeSections.exists_bijective_degreeNToGlobalSections` are
supplied: the kernel is finitely generated by `𝒜₊`-power torsion homogeneous elements because `M`
is a Noetherian module, and `⨁_{n ≥ 0} Γ(Proj 𝒜, M(n)~)` is a finite `A`-module by assertion (1)
of [Stacks, Tag 0B5R] in the degree-one case, so it has finitely many homogeneous generators,
each of which a power of the irrelevant ideal carries into the image of `M`. -/
theorem exists_bijective_degreeNToGlobalSections_degreeOne [IsNoetherianRing (𝒜 0)]
    [Module.Finite A M] {nx : ℕ} (xg : Fin nx → A) (hxg : ∀ i, xg i ∈ 𝒜 1)
    (hxgen : Algebra.adjoin (𝒜 0) (Set.range xg) = ⊤) :
    ∃ n₀ : ℤ, ∀ n : ℤ, n₀ ≤ n → Function.Bijective (degreeNToGlobalSections 𝒜 𝒨 n) := by
  obtain ⟨m, yg, hyg, hygen⟩ :=
    Stacks.ProjCoherentDegreeOne.exists_two_le_generators 𝒜 xg hxg hxgen
  have : IsNoetherianRing A := Stacks.ProjCoherentDegreeOne.isNoetherianRing 𝒜 yg hygen
  have hadj1 : Algebra.adjoin (𝒜 0) ((𝒜 1 : Set A)) = ⊤ :=
    Stacks.ProjCoherentDegreeOne.adjoin_degreeOne_eq_top 𝒜 yg hyg hygen
  obtain ⟨ck, x, dx, Nx, hxtors, hxgen'⟩ := exists_kernel_data 𝒜 𝒨 hadj1
  obtain ⟨cq, dy, Ny, y, hytors, hygen'⟩ := exists_cokernel_data 𝒜 𝒨 yg hyg hygen
  exact ProjLargeDegreeSections.exists_bijective_degreeNToGlobalSections 𝒜 𝒨 hadj1
    x dx Nx hxtors hxgen' dy Ny y hytors hygen'

end Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjLargeDegrees

end
